</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 22, 2004 - 12:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Purplegrrl wrote: <BR><i>Some feedback on your site:  <BR>1. Make the font bigger - white on black that small is just crazy  <BR>2. break your content up with more space between each paragraph - makes it easy to skim read, otherwise looks like one massive piece of text.  <BR>3. take the audio off the front page..or at least set it so that ppl can choose to play it if they want to - at work its fine because I run on a wireless cable system but from home on dialup its ridiculously slow and buffers incorrectly with pauses. Not sure if you want more feedback but I have lots.</i> <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll answer in order -- <BR> <BR>1&#41; I&#39;ve experimented with larger text, but I feel it just looks dorky. Also, my monitor resolution is high but I can still read the text just fine even with bright sunlight hitting the screen. &#40;May dad can too -- and he&#39;s 65 and the first to complain about these things!&#41; <BR> <BR>2&#41; The paragraphs on all the pages are already seperated by breaks. Not sure what you&#39;re referring to. <BR> <BR>3&#41; The actual audio file on the main page is pretty small; only about 35KB in size, about the size of a typical page logo. I want everyone to hear it, as it is the best piece of evidence identifying BTK. Sure, some people do have a slow connection...but they are used to waiting for pages to load. I believe the benefits of having the audio automatically load far outweigh the negatives and that most people have an adequate connection speed for it not to be an issue. <BR> <BR>Regarding more feedback, I do appreciate it. Let&#39;s have some more!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
